Replica: a step-by-step rebuild of Articraft, made to understand it.

This project is inspired by, and includes code adapted from, Articraft:

  Articraft
  https://github.com/mattzh72/articraft
  Paper: https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.15187

Articraft is licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0. A copy of that license
is included in LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt. The adapted portions remain under the Apache
License 2.0. Files that contain adapted material carry a notice at the top
("Portions adapted from Articraft ... and modified for this replica").

What was adapted, file by file (all were modified; none is a verbatim copy of a whole
Articraft module):

- sdk/frames.py
  The rules for turning build123d features into joint frames (face normal or axis of
  symmetry, edge tangent or circle normal), from articraft/sdk/frames.py.
- sdk/profiles.py
  rounded_rect_profile and superellipse_profile (names, arguments, formulas), from
  articraft/sdk/_mesh/profiles.py.
- sdk/primitives.py, sdk/solids.py, sdk/sweeps.py, sdk/mesh_geometry.py, sdk/booleans.py
  The public names, arguments and defaults of Articraft's mesh helpers (BoxGeometry ...
  LatheGeometry, LoftGeometry, PipeGeometry, wire_from_points, tube_from_spline_points,
  section_loft, boolean_union ...), the MeshGeometry method set, placement conventions,
  and the lathe shell lip connector (_cap_connector), from articraft/sdk/_mesh/*.
  The geometry code itself was rewritten.
- sdk/kinematics.py
  The loop-closure approach (articulation tree plus closure joints, bounded
  least-squares solve, joints pinned at limits reported in LoopClosureError), from
  articraft/sdk/assembly.py. Rewritten.
- compiler/worker.py, compiler/runner.py, compiler/feedback.py
  The compile design: fresh worker process, runpy, phase progress file, one JSON
  payload, typed compile signals rendered as a <compile_signals> block with response
  rules and repeat detection, and some rule and hint wording, from
  articraft/compiler/* and articraft/agent/workspace/local.py. Rewritten and extended.
- docs/ARTICRAFT_STUDY.md, docs/SHAPE_HELPERS.md
  A study of Articraft with short code excerpts (each 15 lines or fewer) quoted from its
  source for commentary, and an inventory of its mesh helpers.

Everything else (export to URDF/GLB, mimic joints, the walking warm start, the
Windows process-tree handling, the tests, and the examples) was written for this
project.
